WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.996
This is Inkraft: a benchmark
for Swiss social insurance law.

2
00:00:06.696 --> 00:00:11.815
How much is the minimum
full AHV pension per month?

3
00:00:11.815 --> 00:00:16.833
Ask an AI assistant,
and you might hear CHF 1,225.

4
00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:22.453
That was the law until the end of 2024.

5
00:00:22.453 --> 00:00:27.913
Since January 2025, it has been CHF 1,260.

6
00:00:28.613 --> 00:00:32.503
The answer is already written down,
on fedlex.

7
00:00:32.503 --> 00:00:36.600
And German,
French and Italian are equally binding.

8
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:42.216
So each language gets its gold
answer from its own authentic text,

9
00:00:42.216 --> 00:00:44.343
not from a translation.

10
00:00:45.043 --> 00:00:49.415
Inkraft stores the rule
in force on 1 October 2026,

11
00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:51.558
and the rule it replaced.

12
00:00:51.558 --> 00:00:55.930
So we can tell a stale
answer from an invented one.

13
00:00:55.930 --> 00:01:00.988
And saying “I'm not sure”
is scored apart from being wrong.

14
00:01:01.688 --> 00:01:07.493
The first draft has 303 core questions
in German, French and Italian.

15
00:01:07.493 --> 00:01:11.092
Every row links to the exact
version of the law.

16
00:01:11.092 --> 00:01:13.091
Human review is still pending.

17
00:01:13.791 --> 00:01:19.670
Preliminary results, on the unreviewed
draft and graded by rules only:

18
00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:25.340
on rules changed since 2024, Apertus
answers just 6–10 % correctly,

19
00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:28.134
even with the date in the prompt.

20
00:01:28.134 --> 00:01:33.212
We also search the legal corpus
that Apertus was trained on:

21
00:01:33.212 --> 00:01:37.744
does it contain this paragraph,
and in which version?

22
00:01:38.444 --> 00:01:43.090
Before a model answers questions
from citizens, test it on the law.

23
00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:47.838
Inkraft.
Because the law is the answer key.
